<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<title>Podcast kit — {{ paper.name }}</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Roboto+Flex:opsz,wght@8..144,400..700&family=Roboto+Serif:opsz,wght@8..144,500..800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Material+Symbols+Rounded:opsz,wght,FILL,GRAD@20..48,400,0..1,0&display=block" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ root }}static/style.css?v={{ v }}">
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
{% set ed = None %}
{% include "_masthead.html.j2" %}
<main class="podcast-page kit" id="feed">
  <h1>Podcast kit</h1>
  <p class="pod-intro">Covers: {% if d.start == d.end %}{{ d.end_l }}{% else %}{{ d.start_l }} to {{ d.end_l }}{% endif %} · {{ d.count }} stories. About five minutes of your time.</p>
  <ol class="kit-steps">
    <li>Download <a href="sources.txt" download="tone-at-the-top-week-{{ d.end }}.txt"><b>the sources file</b></a>.</li>
    <li>Open <a href="https://notebooklm.google.com">NotebookLM</a>, create a new notebook and upload the file as its only source (or add this page as a Website source: <code>{{ paper.site_url }}podcast/kit/{{ d.end }}.html</code>).</li>
    <li>In Studio, open <b>Audio Overview → Customize</b> and choose: {% for k, val in settings %}<b>{{ k }}</b> {{ val }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</li>
    <li>Paste this into the prompt box and press Generate:
      <div class="kit-prompt"><p id="prompt">{{ prompt }}</p><button type="button" class="kit-copy" data-copy="prompt"><span class="ms" aria-hidden="true">content_copy</span>Copy prompt</button></div></li>
    <li>Listen to the start and end to check it, then use <b>⋮ → Download</b>. It saves a WAV file.</li>
    <li><a class="kit-btn" href="{{ upload }}"><span class="ms" aria-hidden="true">upload</span>Upload the episode</a> Drag the file onto that page and press <b>Publish release</b>. The site and the next morning email update automatically within a few minutes.</li>
  </ol>
</main>
</div>
<script>document.querySelectorAll('.kit-copy').forEach(function(b){b.addEventListener('click',function(){var t=document.getElementById(b.dataset.copy).textContent;(navigator.clipboard?navigator.clipboard.writeText(t):Promise.reject()).then(function(){b.lastChild.textContent='Copied';},function(){});});});</script>
</body>
</html>
